Decisions embodied for Michael's review:
1. One active plan container per pasture may hold multiple dividers.
2. Each divider may have ordered interior waypoints.
3. Combined plan geometry determines the current derived regions and acreages.
4. Shared interior junctions use explicit many-divider references, atomic whole-plan
   revalidation, restricted deletion, and reference-safe archival/orphan cleanup.
5. Waypoint/junction promotion and demotion require explicit guarded operations with
   atomic reference updates; spatial overlap never changes node identity.
6. Existing 1.2.0 straight plans migrate without redraw.
7. Field Log uses seven Track & Trace-derived categories but native RangeWater storage,
   precise placement, task state, map presentation, archive safety, and backup semantics.
8. Permanent pasture conversion and parcel lookup remain deferred.

